        <UserObject label="" mermaidData="{&#xa;  &quot;data&quot;: &quot;sequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Parent as Parent (User)\n    participant Client as Frontend (App/Web)\n    participant API as Backend API (FastAPI)\n    participant DB as Database (PostgreSQL)\n    participant Resend as Email Service (Resend)\n\n    Note over Parent, Resend: Email Registration &amp; Duplicate Check Workflow\n\n    Parent-&gt;&gt;Client: 1. Enter Name, Email, and Password\n    Client-&gt;&gt;API: 2. POST /api/auth/register\n    \n    API-&gt;&gt;DB: 3. SELECT * FROM parents WHERE email = input_email\n    DB--&gt;&gt;API: 4. Return query result\n\n    alt Case A: Email is Unique (Success)\n        DB--&gt;&gt;API: No existing user found\n        API-&gt;&gt;API: 5. Hash Password (bcrypt/argon2)\n        API-&gt;&gt;DB: 6. INSERT INTO parents (email, password_hash, ...)\n        DB--&gt;&gt;API: 7. Success: User Created\n        \n        par Parallel Execution\n            API--&gt;&gt;Client: 8. HTTP 201 Created (Return JWT Token)\n            Client--&gt;&gt;Parent: 9. Registration Success &amp; Login\n        and Async Background Task\n            API-)Resend: 10. Send Verification Email Link\n            Resend--)Parent: 11. Delivery: \&quot;Verify your email\&quot;\n        end\n\n    else Case B: Email Already Exists (Conflict)\n        DB--&gt;&gt;API: User record already exists\n        API--&gt;&gt;Client: 5. HTTP 409 Conflict (\&quot;Email already exists\&quot;)\n        Client--&gt;&gt;Parent: 6. Show error message &amp; provide login redirect\n    end\n&quot;,&#xa;  &quot;config&quot;: null,&#xa;  &quot;version&quot;: &quot;12&quot;&#xa;}" id="ewKjAh-1ta5-ABaI637t-1">
